\begin_layout Abstract
Time-Dependent Density Functional Theory (TD-DFT) is used to generate the
 transition probability of electrons from valence band (VB) to conduction
 band (CB) in indirect band-gap semiconductor Si.
 Two orientations of crystalline lattice are compared.
 Typical pulses used in laser applications are built using a space of 7
 tuning parameters, including wavelength, pulse duration, phases inside
 the envelope, and the polarization of laser fields.
 Purpose of this document is for now to analyze and keep a trace of first
 quantum simulations.
 This is aimed to prepare a paper on the non-linear absorption of light
 by Si atoms exposed to single-color and bi-color laser excitations.
 
\end_layout

